 "text": "9/30/26, 5:12 AM\n\nSAP Business Partner\n\nThe SAP Business Partner represents an organization (company, branch), person, or group of persons or organizations in which\nyour company has a business interest.\n\nBusiness partners used in Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable must exist in the Contract Partner role MKK.\nYou can enter and manage your business partners centrally with regard to different business transactions.\nThis is particularly useful if a business partner plays different roles in an enterprise, such as a payer as well as a service recipient.\n\nA business partner can be created in various business partner roles and can assume additional business partner roles during the\ncourse of the business relationship. You do not have to enter the general data for a business partner each time, which avoids\nredundant data entry and retention.\n\nStructure\n\nThe following basic elements are available in the business partner data:\n\nConcept                                                                                                        Comment\n\nBusiness partner category                                                             The data available for your business transactions depends on the\nbusiness partner category.\n\nBusiness partner role                                                                  A business partner can take on different business partner roles,\nwhich enable different views of the business partner data\ndepending on the business function.\n\nBusiness partner relationship                                                      A relationship connects two business partners and is identified by\nthe business partner relationship category .\n\nBusiness partner group hierarchy                                                 You can use the business partner group hierarchy to represent the\nstructure of an organization.\n\nRelated Information\n\nSAP Business Partner\n\nBusiness Partner in the Contract Partner Role (MKK)\n\nUse\n\nYou use the business partner in Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable in the role of the contract partner (MKK).\n\nA contract partner is connected with the company through contract accounts and through the conclusion of contracts. Contract\naccounts can therefore only be assigned to a business partner and services billed accordingly if you have created this business\npartner in the role of contract partner in the business role MKK for role category MKK.\n",
